{number: 157}
{title: I Just Keep Trusting My Lord}
{key: G}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[G] I just keep trusting my Lord as I walk a-[D7] long;
I just keep trusting my Lord, and He gives a [G] song.
Though the storm clouds darken the sky o'er the [C] heav'nly trail,
I just [G] keep on trusting my [D7] Lord, He will never [G] fail.
He's a [C] faithful Friend, such a [G] faithful Friend;
He's a [D7] faithful Friend on whom I can de-[G] pend.
Though the storm clouds darken the sky o'er the [C] heav'nly trail,
I just [G] keep on trusting my [D7] Lord, He will never [G] fail.
{end_of_verse}
